# Wednesday's rulings on the gate86 kit (KIT_REPORT.md §6), to be read WHOLE by the gate seat

Carried from the gate85 kit's RULINGS_wednesday.md and the gate84 / gate82 rulings it carried, and from the gate86 commission (a TIER-2 BATCH of FOUR PRs, tier 2 proposed by Seat F 16th, the gate decides each tier). Nothing below was invented by the kit builder except where a line says "NOT RULED" (and then it carries its DEFAULT). **There is NO "RULED at launch" block yet: Wednesday adds one (back this file up as `RULINGS_wednesday.md.pre-launch` first).** Where this file is absent the gate uses the DEFAULTs in KIT_REPORT.

## Carried and still applying

- **The gate never edits, merges, comments on tickets or messages humans.** It never mails a builder seat. Its work ends at the verdict mail to Wednesday. It never edits a PR body: the LIVE bodies ARE the builders' Test Evidence (kit pins sha256/16 `4e5a48c1ae49cdc5` #1451, `8885d2e7c7200bd3` #1452, `60cadb372e3199b8` #1454, `2516a74ebdb9588e` #1455); they are judged and reported, never changed.
- **ONE verdict per PR (GO or NO GO) at that PR's pinned head**, FOUR verdict lines plus a composition line. A head that moved at the gate's START reading is **NOT RUN** for that PR (no verdict); a head that moves later voids that PR's verdict. The batch is gated as one gate but a moved head does not void the other three unless the composition depended on it (say so).
- **MERGE ADDENDUM, LAST in report.md:** one line per PR plus the composition line. The proposed squash subject carries **no `(#n)`**: the declared subject is the landed subject byte for byte, at most 92 characters as declared, and TRUE of the diff.
- **Docs composition (carried from gate81..gate85):** every PR appends a flow block and a cheat section immediately before the closing `</body>\n</html>\n` of the two platform-k HTML docs; **all four share that anchor with each other and with the landed block `57.`**, and #1451 / #1452 both regenerate `secuura-api.yaml`. **The keep-both is the LATER MERGE SEAT's job, never any PR's and never the gate's on the real branches**; the gate PREDICTS it in its OWN clone (c3 `compose`) and proves the result with a per-block COUNT, `html_docs_matrix` (blind to a dropped AND a duplicated block) and `generate-openapi --check`. Renumbering is the merge seat's call.
- **Pre-existing CI (carried):** GitHub Actions IS EXECUTING on PRs (the CLAUDE.md "retired for billing" note is stale). `Security Scanning` (KS-1148: `audit-locks.mjs` imports undeclared `semver`) is known; other reds are classified by JOB and STEP against develop's OWN push runs at the develop the gate reads. The gate **verifies every attribution** and does **not count a verified pre-existing red against any PR**. A red it cannot classify from the log BLOCKS. NOT RUN is never a pass; a run still in progress is UNMEASURED, never green.
- **An image-pull / infrastructure red (gate82 Q-INFRA1449, a single-instance pilot):** the gate quotes the log line and says it cannot re-run a job; infrastructure is attributable only on that quoted evidence.
- **Q-ATTR (carried):** the `Generated with` line is COUNTED and reported, not ruled (gate77 Q-ATTR77 precedent). Each body carries 1.
- **Q-DOCKER (carried):** no Docker; the four platform suites NOT RUN / NOT COMMISSIONED (`docker info` once, quote rc, never start Docker).
- **Q-MODEL (carried):** the exec line carries no `--model`; Wednesday types `/model claude-opus-5-5` at the gate's idle prompt.
- **Q-CLASS / Q-HOOKS-SIBLINGS (carried):** a class sibling or a prediction slip found by the gate is reported only; Wednesday routes it via a board seat after a search.
- **Holds kept:** never touch the shared checkout's `core.hooksPath`; no board writes; findings only, never fixes. Every instrument takes `--develop` as a REQUIRED argument (the develop the gate read) and, new here, `--base` PER PR.

## Gate notes added by the coordinator (task brief to the kit builder, 2026-10-11)

- The batch: #1451 (KS-591, A1, six POST bodies declared required, flow 55), #1452 (KS-1364, B2, five bodies, flow 56), #1454 (KS-1355, C2, dev-reload.sh names the slot container, flow 58, PARTIAL for the ticket) and #1455 (KS-1417 piece 2, D1, env.local.example, flow 59, ONE declared deviation from the Spark payload). All ours; develop at the draft `e27b9dceff390d8048e8970efd2eab15f21b01fe`; heads read by `ls-remote` at about 18:2x AEDT 2026-10-11 and re-read at launch.
- The handler behaviour behind the required-body declarations is UNMEASURED by the builders; the platform suites need a local stack and are UNMEASURED; #1454 and #1455 owe live runs / a fresh-clone bootstrap.
- Known collision to MODEL, not to fix: the docs tails (all four + the landed 57) and the yaml (#1451 / #1452); the gate predicts the merge-in and checks the order-independence of the four doc blocks.

## OPEN items, each with its DEFAULT (OPEN means the kit builder could not derive it from a file)

- **Q-SEAT86 (merge seat): NOT RULED, NO DEFAULT.** The launch takes `--seat "Seat X nth"`; the FOUR GO strings `GO (<seat>): merge <n> on gate86` are derived from it and the launcher refuses (rc 8) if the prompt disagrees or `@MERGE_SEAT@` survives. A dry-run seat is a test value, not a ruling.
- **Q-TIER86 (verdict subject tag): NOT RULED. DEFAULT `GATE86 (T2)`** for the whole batch (the seat proposed T2 for all four); the gate records each PR's tier in a body line and DISAGREEs where it must.
- **Q-NM86 (how the gate gets node_modules for #1451 / #1452 and the composed trees): NOT RULED. DEFAULT: a read-only `cp -R` from the builders' worktrees `worktrees/s-f12-ks591/Blockchain/Dev` (#1451 and the composed trees) and `worktrees/s-f13-b2/Blockchain/Dev` (#1452)**, `nmcheck`-verified (0 mismatches at the draft). **This relaxes "never touch a builder's worktree" to a READ and needs your word** (the same default gate85 asked for with s-f14-c1). If a worktree is gone at launch the vitest-based checks of that PR are NOT RUN with the blocker named. The copies took ~75 s and 1.5 GB each at the draft.
- **Q-X9 (the #1455 suite names env.example / bootstrap-env.sh): NOT RULED. DEFAULT: allowed, ONLY through `c3 shell --pr 1455` from a scratch tree outside every repo** (the suite copies the bootstrap script into its own mktemp tree and `cd`s there first; the drafter ran it that way, 6/0 at head, 5/1 at the base template). The gate85 hold ("no shell suite that names env.example") is otherwise kept.
- **Q-ORDER86 (merge order): DEFAULT #1451, #1452, #1454, #1455** (flow 55, 56, 58, 59 in increasing document order after the landed 57); the composition is order-independent in content (24 orders, one non-doc state, one yaml blob), so the order only fixes the document order of the appended blocks.
- **Q-HANDLER86 (may the gate probe the handlers' absent-body behaviour?): DEFAULT yes**, with its own vitest file written INTO a scratch tree (named exception X1), real route code with stubbed dependencies; otherwise NOT RUN.
- **Q-LINE79-86 (#1454's title vs the unbraced `$CONTAINER…` line): DEFAULT: the gate measures it and rules severity; Minor BLOCKS no if the PR body already says the line-73 (now 79) defect is not in this change, Major if the title is untrue in the default locale and the body does not say so.**
- **Q-KS991-86 (hyphenated `KS-991` in the #1452 and #1454 bodies, kit `prtext` T3 FAIL): DEFAULT: Polish BLOCKS no if it is inside a quoted hook line, Minor otherwise; the body is never edited by the gate.**
- **Q-STREAM86:** the test-block stream parent (KS-485 for #1451 / #1452 per the builders; none for #1454 / #1455) is yours to name.
- **Q-DEVCI86:** the gate classifies develop's push-run reds by job and step. **Q-PROMPT86:** the prompt has had no reader but the drafter and the launcher's `--check`. **Q-CHARTER86:** the drafter read the gate85 kit WHOLE, BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md WHOLE and QA_AGENT_CHARTER.md WHOLE; it did NOT read STANDING_LINES.md whole.
